 oil & gas storage, building products, home entertainment, B2B, consumer electronics, home supply store, lodging, commercial services & supplies, metal & mineral mining machinery, coal, hazardous waste collection, solid waste collection, waste water treatment, renewable electricity, equity REITs, power generation by nuclear & fossil fuels, personal loan services, chemicals, other specialty retail, biotech, pharmaceuticals, metal, aerospace, healthcare, cable, entertainment services, infrastructure services, transportation infrastructure, exhaust, life sciences, alternative carriers, infrastructure, system software, manufacturing services, enterprise tech and consumer, enterprise software & application, as well as consumer technologies. The firm considers investment in Asia, Latin America, Japan, Australia, South Korea, Singapore, Hong Kong, Africa, Middle East, Beijing, Shanghai, India, Belgium, France, Ireland, Luxembourg, Monaco, Netherlands, United Kingdom, North America and South America. It seeks to invest between $0.25 million and $900 million per transaction. It invests in companies with enterprise value between $500 million and $5000 million. It makes equity investments up to $300 million through fund of fund investments. It has a three year investment period. The firm prefers to take majority and minority stakes. Its hedge fund business manages a broad range of commingled and customized fund solutions and its credit business focuses on loans, and securities of non-investment grade companies spread across the capital structure including senior debt, subordinated debt, preferred stock and common equity. Blackstone Inc. through its subsidiary South City Projects (Kolkata) Limited offers residential and commercial real estate development services that include development of township, residential towers, malls, IT parks, stadiums, resorts, hospitals, and schools. Blackstone Inc. was founded in 1985 and is based in New York, New York with additional offices across Asia, Europe, North America and Central America.", "market_cap": null, "shares_outstanding": null, "next_earnings_date": "2026-10-22", "eps_estimate_avg": 1.37204, "eps_estimate_num": 16, "eps_estimate_growth": -0.0973, "eps_estimate_fwd": 7.45502, "revenue_estimate_avg": 3399833330.0, "eps_revisions_up_30d": 3, "eps_revisions_down_30d": 10, "is_active": true, "market_code": "NYSE", "region": "us"}, "tradingview_symbol": "NYSE:BX", "quote": {"security_id": 533, "price": 134.68, "prev_close": 126.46, "change": 8.22, "change_pct": 6.500079, "day_open": 125.199997, "day_high": 135.21, "day_low": 128.0, "volume": 4674074, "quoted_at": "2026-07-27T12:50:17.125760", "eps_ttm": 3.87, "pe_ttm": 34.8}, "scores": {"id": 63, "security_id": 533, "as_of": "2026-07-27", "fundamental": 69.04, "technical": 60.35, "momentum": 60.41, "quality": 95.03, "risk": 62.15, "composite": 68.3, "pabrai": 59.9, "breakdown": {"fundamental": {"score": 69.04, "coverage": 0.75, "weight_present": 0.75, "metrics": {"roe": {"label": "Return on equity", "value": 0.357772, "sub_score": 100.0, "weight": 0.14, "contribution": 14.0}, "net_margin": {"label": "Net margin", "value": 0.243289, "sub_score": 100.0, "weight": 0.1, "contribution": 10.0}, "roa": {"label": "Return on assets", "value": 0.066226, "sub_score": 55.19, "weight": 0.08, "contribution": 4.4152}, "revenue_growth": {"label": "Revenue growth", "value": 0.135352, "sub_score": 67.24, "weight": 0.1, "contribution": 6.724}, "eps_growth": {"label": "EPS growth", "value": 0.069061, "sub_score": 42.27, "weight": 0.1, "contribution": 4.227}, "debt_to_equity": {"label": "Debt / equity", "value": 1.535529, "sub_score": 38.58, "weight": 0.1, "contribution": 3.858}, "fcf_margin": {"label": "Free-cash-flow margin", "value": 0.366435, "sub_score": 100.0, "weight": 0.05, "contribution": 5.0}, "piotroski_f": {"label": "Piotroski F-Score", "value": 4.0, "sub_score": 44.44, "weight": 0.08, "contribution": 3.5552}}, "missing": ["gross_margin", "current_ratio",